  "details": "Official YouTube playback in VRChat depends on VRChat’s bundled yt-dlp. When YouTube changes extractors or bot checks, Public and Group Public instances lose YouTube for days or weeks until VRChat ships an update.\n\nWorld-level “Video Player Allowed Domains” does not cover this well:\n\n- only the world creator can add a host\n\n- cap is 10 domains (which I do genuinely believe is quite small but that is a separate point)\n\n- every club/bar world has to opt in separately\n\n- a new instance is required after a change to the list\n\nuwu.tv is a stream service for VRChat video players (PC and Quest). Users paste a normal YouTube/Twitch URL or use a short https://uwu.tv/… link. Quest gets 720p H.264 and PC can get 1080p when supported. (As always this depends on the video)\n\nHost for the allowlist: uwu.tv\n\nLinks\n\n- Site: https://uwu.tv/\n\n- Privacy: https://uwu.tv/privacy\n\n- Terms: https://uwu.tv/terms\n\nThis is simply meant as a fallback for world creators and instances and not a replacement to VRChat's currenty Youtube Implementation, putting uwu.tv on the global list would make that fallback work in Public / Group Public without each creator burning a slot, or additional delays during these outages such as the last few weeks, simply copy pasting the youtube url on top of https://uwu.tv would bridge the gap during these times.\n\nHappy to add an abuse contact or any other trust requirement if that is the blocker, and any feedback or suggestion is appreciated.",
